# Design Freeze

Once a UI milestone has been approved and committed, that Git commit becomes
the canonical design reference.

**Current Adaptive Workspace / Person Workspace baseline:** `32fd0f8`
(“Adaptive Workspace foundation and Person Workspace UI polish”), as amended
by explicit UI milestones (currently **BP-036D** — permanent desktop split:
nav left + active workspace right).

## Rules

- Future milestones may **NOT** modify approved layouts unless the milestone
  explicitly authorizes UI work.
- Any unrelated UI modification is a **regression** — revert it to the
  approved commit for those files.
- Do not reinterpret, modernize, or “improve” frozen layouts during data-model,
  backend, or non-UI milestones.
- When restoring UI, prefer restoring exact file contents from the canonical
  commit rather than re-implementing from memory.

## Scope (Person Workspace)

Frozen surfaces include Workspace Navigation, Adaptive Workspace panel,
workspace switching, Executive Overview layout, Tennis Performance layout,
and related sizing / positioning / spacing / typography.
